                <pb facs="0998" n="958" xml:id="pg958"/>


                <head>Basic Financial Statistics—Israel</head>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">I. Bond Drive (Unclassified)</hi></p>
                <p>From May 1, 1952, the initial date of the bond flotation, to December 31, 1951:
                        <table cols="2" rows="2">
                        <row>
                            <cell>Subscriptions</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$101,647,300</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Cash receipts</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$54,100,000</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table></p>
                <p>The most recent data available indicate that the totals had been increased to:
                        <table cols="2" rows="2">
                        <row>
                            <cell>Subscriptions (May 1952)</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$125,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Cash receipts (June 1952)</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$75,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table></p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">II. United Jewish Appeal
                        (Unclassified)</hi></p>
                <p>Collections in the United States since 1948: <table cols="2" rows="6">
                        <row role="label">
                            <cell>1948</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$148,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>1949</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$116,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>1950</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$90,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>1951</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$85,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>1952 (five months)</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$39,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Total</cell>
                            <cell role="num">$478,000,000</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Note:</hi> An unofficial Israel source estimates that
                    three-quarters of these collections accrued to Israel and the remainder was used
                    for Jews outside Israel.</p>
